<article class="env-remark" id="190928">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/190928">Remark <span data-tag="190928">8.3.1.6</span>.</a> An easy formal argument shows that condition $(2)$ is equivalent to either of the following statements: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2')$"><p>
Given any cofibration $i: D \rightarrow D'$ in ${\mathbf A}$ and any fibration $j: X \rightarrow Y$ in ${\mathbf A}$, the induced map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ k: \bHom _{{\mathbf A}}(D',X) \rightarrow \bHom _{{\mathbf A}}(D,X) \times _{ \bHom _{{\mathbf A}}(D,Y)} \bHom _{{\mathbf A}}(D',Y) \]
</div>
<p>
 is fibration in ${\mathbf S}$, which is trivial if either $i$ or $j$ is a weak equivalence. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2'')$"><p>
Given any cofibration $i: C \rightarrow C'$ in ${\mathbf S}$ and any fibration $j: X \rightarrow Y$ in ${\mathbf A}$, the induced map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ k: X^{C'} \rightarrow X^ C \times _{ Y^ C} Y^{C'} \]
</div>
<p>
 is a fibration in ${\mathbf A}$, which is trivial if either $i$ or $j$ is trivial. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>